1
00:01:06,820 --> 00:02:02,440
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:06,970
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION.

3
00:02:25,090 --> 00:02:28,180
That's how my father sees fit, Osman Bey.

4
00:02:28,820 --> 00:02:31,710
Allah is with those who have patience.

5
00:02:37,510 --> 00:02:39,740
May I come in, son?

6
00:02:42,970 --> 00:02:45,820
I wish to be alone, aunt.

7
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:18,280
Aren't you alone in a crowded place, if you
can't be together with your loved one, son?

8
00:03:19,870 --> 00:03:23,650
Does it matter if I'm here or not?

9
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:40,290
My heart aches every time
I think about it.

10
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:45,410
Why doesn't he see me worthy
of his daughter?

11
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:49,080
What did I do wrong for him
to not see me as a man?

12
00:03:50,290 --> 00:03:52,870
It's not about being a man, son.

13
00:03:52,870 --> 00:03:58,910
Sheikh Edebali knows your manliness, your
courage the best.

14
00:04:01,210 --> 00:04:05,210
What really matters is what
you're going to do now.

15
00:04:07,350 --> 00:04:11,080
Will you let your anger get
the better of you...

16
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:15,060
... or will you overcome it and
proceed with your mind?

17
00:04:18,440 --> 00:04:21,570
That's what this is all about.

18
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:50,480
It looks like winter will be harsh.

19
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:55,080
We need to work hard. We also need to take
care of the poor.

20
00:04:55,080 --> 00:05:01,250
We shall prepare the shoes, hats, and
vests to be handed out.

21
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:05,870
We'll get through this if Allah permits.

22
00:05:13,450 --> 00:05:15,360
It's okay.

23
00:05:16,350 --> 00:05:18,720
It didn't burn, don't worry.

24
00:05:21,180 --> 00:05:25,180
No visible burns, but...

25
00:05:25,180 --> 00:05:27,270
... the fire is deep inside.

26
00:05:29,150 --> 00:05:34,710
Bala. Every cloud has a silver lining.

27
00:05:36,330 --> 00:05:39,760
What matters is seeing the good in
my Sheikh's decision.

28
00:05:51,110 --> 00:05:55,110
I don't know the reason or the outcome of
this decision.

29
00:05:57,410 --> 00:06:01,870
I only know one thing.
My heart pumps for Osman now.

30
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:11,250
If I have to wait, I shall spend
my life waiting.

31
00:06:13,960 --> 00:06:20,330
Waiting is tough, but it's worth it
if I'm waiting for Osman.

32
00:06:28,650 --> 00:06:33,420
If we're talking about Osman, you won't be
waiting for long.

33
00:06:34,710 --> 00:06:37,530
He'll find a way.

34
00:06:40,560 --> 00:06:43,890
It's a weird feeling.

35
00:06:45,940 --> 00:06:50,230
It's snowing on me, but my insides
are burning.

36
00:06:53,570 --> 00:06:59,190
I don't know if I'm cold, or if I'm
burning. But my father has the answers.

37
00:07:00,020 --> 00:07:02,480
I'll go talk to him.

38
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:19,860
- Welcome, my daughter.
- Thank you, father.

39
00:07:21,830 --> 00:07:25,280
Nights are longer now, I thought you
might be hungry.

40
00:07:25,980 --> 00:07:30,130
Thank you, that's nice of you, my Bala.

41
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:39,280
It's important to know the right time, to
wait for the right time.

42
00:08:33,360 --> 00:08:40,020
In these lands, almond trees bloom, all
of a sudden...

43
00:08:40,020 --> 00:08:44,290
... thinking the spring has come, my
daughter.

44
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:52,630
They get fooled by the fake sunlight, and
by the warmth of the branches.

45
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:05,700
But instead, because it wasn't the right
time, all they get is the night's cold.

46
00:09:14,590 --> 00:09:17,900
Time is also important in relationships.

47
00:09:19,410 --> 00:09:24,750
You shall protect your fresh leaves,
your essence that I worked hard on...

48
00:09:24,750 --> 00:09:27,620
... from the winter sun.

49
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:35,370
Protect them, so that winter's cold
can't burn your flowers.

50
00:09:39,410 --> 00:09:42,960
I don't want you to talk to Osman.

51
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:47,570
Remember that.

52
00:10:35,150 --> 00:10:37,470
Bala!

53
00:10:39,210 --> 00:10:43,210
What happened, Bala? Are you okay?

54
00:10:46,400 --> 00:10:51,410
My father doesn't want me to
talk with Osman.

55
00:10:52,930 --> 00:10:56,070
He has made his decision, Gonca.

56
00:11:00,380 --> 00:11:02,540
He has made his decision.

57
00:11:20,350 --> 00:11:25,880
Once upon a time, there was a beautiful
young lady, and a brave young man.

58
00:11:28,110 --> 00:11:32,710
My Rab made them meet each
other using a deer.

59
00:11:34,370 --> 00:11:39,630
They fell in love the moment they saw
each other.

60
00:11:41,820 --> 00:11:47,210
I can't tell you all of them, son. They
fought such troubles.

61
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:53,680
But they never gave up on their love.

62
00:11:55,830 --> 00:12:02,710
That love came to life, became three
brave little valiants.

63
00:12:03,720 --> 00:12:07,900
Gündüz, Savcı, and you.

64
00:12:09,970 --> 00:12:18,200
Now how can you be upset like that?
Tell me.

65
00:12:19,190 --> 00:12:22,280
My heart is a battlefield, aunt.

66
00:12:24,650 --> 00:12:28,650
My loved one is besides me, but
I can't pull her closer.

67
00:12:32,130 --> 00:12:36,410
It's not anger, not greed.

68
00:12:38,070 --> 00:12:40,570
But...

69
00:12:42,050 --> 00:12:44,800
Not being able to come together
drives me crazy.

70
00:12:53,740 --> 00:12:56,060
May I come in, my Bey?

71
00:12:59,810 --> 00:13:02,140
Come in, Konur Alp.

72
00:13:18,020 --> 00:13:20,840
My Bey...

73
00:13:21,890 --> 00:13:25,540
Your fires hurt me as well.

74
00:13:26,550 --> 00:13:30,550
I couldn't stay in the Alp Tent,
I came here.

75
00:13:31,890 --> 00:13:35,690
Give the orders, and we shall
take off, my Bey.

76
00:13:37,830 --> 00:13:43,930
Since she also loves you, let's kidnap
Bala Hatun, my Bey.

77
00:14:06,820 --> 00:14:12,290
I like disorder but everything got
out of hand this time.

78
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:16,590
In this chaos, the biggest duty
is yours, Sofia.

79
00:14:30,850 --> 00:14:34,320
As long as our aims win, father.

80
00:14:34,490 --> 00:14:39,900
Alişar is the only power who can
defeat Kayıs without using weapons.

81
00:14:40,420 --> 00:14:43,960
For this reason, his allience is crucial.

82
00:14:44,910 --> 00:14:48,120
Don't tire yourself anymore, sir.

83
00:14:50,150 --> 00:14:53,180
What you're trying to say is understood.

84
00:15:43,110 --> 00:15:48,020
May others help you as well, son.

85
00:15:50,450 --> 00:15:54,880
Your grandsons shall respect you too, son.

86
00:15:55,420 --> 00:15:58,440
Thank you, my Bey father.
May Allah accept your prayers.

87
00:15:59,340 --> 00:16:02,110
Is there anything wrong
in the Tent, Yaman?

88
00:16:02,180 --> 00:16:07,260
Everything is fine, my Bey.
But I heard something at night.

89
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:15,850
You, my Yaman, stay still like an owl, but
you don't miss a single thing.

90
00:16:15,850 --> 00:16:18,860
Tell me, what is it?

91
00:16:18,860 --> 00:16:24,890
Osman has sent Selcan Hatun to ask Sheikh
Edebali permission to marry his daughter.

92
00:16:31,040 --> 00:16:33,600
What did he say?

93
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:38,470
Didn't allow it.
Sheikh Edebali didn't even bother.

94
00:16:43,050 --> 00:16:49,960
That's what happens if you send your
aunt, instead of your Tent's Bey uncle.

95
00:16:50,820 --> 00:16:54,820
Now Osman can cry on his own.

96
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:59,240
- May I come in, uncle?
- Come in, my nephew.

97
00:17:05,180 --> 00:17:09,420
Is it good news, this early in
the morning?

98
00:17:09,420 --> 00:17:13,330
A caravan's status came in from our
scout Alps along the border.

99
00:17:14,050 --> 00:17:18,050
Departed from Nikea, I suppose they
are going to Kulucahisar.

100
00:17:18,960 --> 00:17:23,790
The good news keeps on coming.
Are they loaded?

101
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:26,460
Carrier-full.

102
00:17:26,460 --> 00:17:33,400
They are trying to hide it but, they are
ready for battle.

103
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:36,700
Do you think they are preparing
for battle, my Bey?

104
00:17:36,700 --> 00:17:44,400
Silently. They smile at our faces, but
they are preparing for battle.

105
00:17:44,930 --> 00:17:49,770
- What is your order?
- It's certain...

106
00:17:49,770 --> 00:17:54,610
... that everyone shows their
true colours, my nephew.

107
00:17:56,140 --> 00:18:01,350
- So will we.
- Are we, going to attack the castle?

108
00:18:01,350 --> 00:18:07,500
No. Not now. Not now

109
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:14,180
First, we'll attack the caravan and
strangle the castle for a little while.

110
00:18:14,640 --> 00:18:18,430
They think Dündar Bey forgot.

111
00:18:18,430 --> 00:18:23,780
But they don't know that
I don't forget anything!

112
00:18:24,640 --> 00:18:31,950
Kidnapping my daughter and torturing
Osman. They will pay for both of them.

113
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:37,270
- They will pay for it.
- I should tell Osman to prepare with his Alps.

114
00:18:37,270 --> 00:18:41,370
No no. No need.

115
00:18:45,310 --> 00:18:50,120
My brave son Batur will take care of this.

116
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:55,510
We don't attack the enemy in
such a way lately.

117
00:18:55,510 --> 00:19:01,880
Now go and show them who
Dündar Bey's son Batur Alp is.

118
00:19:02,560 --> 00:19:08,700
Bring the bounty here so Kayı Beys
see a valiant!

119
00:19:08,860 --> 00:19:11,330
Your wish is my command, my Bey.

120
00:19:36,220 --> 00:19:45,280
Friends, it's now obvious that before
we destroy the evil in Kulucahisar...

121
00:19:45,280 --> 00:19:48,060
... we can't rest in these lands.

122
00:19:49,380 --> 00:19:51,470
Are we going to migrate, my Sheikh?

123
00:19:51,470 --> 00:19:56,940
We'll make these lands our
country, Zülfikar.

124
00:19:58,900 --> 00:20:02,100
We'll go for a fight.

125
00:20:02,100 --> 00:20:07,160
Surviving in these lands is tough, my
Sheikh. One needs strong allies.

126
00:20:07,590 --> 00:20:13,260
Banner Lord Alişar is Konya's man
from the Mongolian attacks.

127
00:20:14,010 --> 00:20:18,620
While Ertuğrul Bey isn't here, Dündar Bey
won't side with us.

128
00:20:19,870 --> 00:20:22,140
Osman on the other hand...

129
00:20:22,140 --> 00:20:25,730
And we didn't let Osman marry
our daughter.

130
00:20:25,730 --> 00:20:29,100
Who are we going to do this with, you're
saying, right Fakı?

131
00:20:30,340 --> 00:20:34,340
I couldn't say it myself, master.
That's what we lack.

132
00:20:37,790 --> 00:20:44,380
We don't ask for anyone's approval. Only
Allah giveth.

133
00:20:45,900 --> 00:20:50,270
For this reason, we'll move to Yenipazar.

134
00:20:52,400 --> 00:20:56,720
As stronger, more stable.

135
00:20:57,800 --> 00:21:01,640
We'll let Muslims breathe with
our craftsmanship.

136
00:21:03,410 --> 00:21:05,690
- Pehlivan.
- Yes, sir.

137
00:21:05,690 --> 00:21:08,290
- Zülfikar.
- Yes, my Sheikh.

138
00:21:08,620 --> 00:21:14,640
Send the news to Tekeli, Konya, and
Kayseri.

139
00:21:14,640 --> 00:21:23,760
They shall wake up. Our friends with Ahi's
spirit in their hearts shall get on the road.

140
00:21:24,400 --> 00:21:31,290
It's time for us to bless these wild
grass-covered lands with roses of faith.

141
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:35,100
- Yes, my Sheikh.
- Yes, master.

142
00:21:48,350 --> 00:21:52,660
Do you see the silks, the cloths?

143
00:21:52,660 --> 00:21:56,630
- Suits my Bey well.
- Same with the ones in the castle.

144
00:21:57,540 --> 00:22:03,560
Alişar Bey's mansion is no different
from a palace. Right, Nizamettin?

145
00:22:03,560 --> 00:22:05,670
Correct, my Bey.

146
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:09,990
Why are you upset?

147
00:22:09,990 --> 00:22:13,350
Your Beylic's intentions are no good.

148
00:22:17,990 --> 00:22:22,950
What are you talking about? What do you
mean they are no good?

149
00:22:23,390 --> 00:22:28,360
While you were in Konya, Osman and
Kulucahisar issue reignited.

150
00:22:29,570 --> 00:22:33,100
Nizamettin, Nizamettin.

151
00:22:33,710 --> 00:22:39,080
You think you're gathering news. I know
what Osman is doing.

152
00:22:39,370 --> 00:22:45,530
I know about the rest. Osman's Alps died.
His intentions are certain.

153
00:22:46,150 --> 00:22:49,610
Killing Sofia and Kalonoz.

154
00:22:49,610 --> 00:22:53,510
And, my Bey, Sofia wants to visit you
in your mansion.

155
00:22:54,180 --> 00:22:57,220
It's obvious that it's about this issue.

156
00:22:58,120 --> 00:23:02,120
I like the silky ones and the
ones with flowers.

157
00:23:03,550 --> 00:23:07,450
Tell the princess she can come.

158
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:19,850
I smell like a goat thanks to all
those migrating ones! Zorba!

159
00:23:20,850 --> 00:23:23,420
Prepare the bathhouse!

160
00:23:49,440 --> 00:23:56,830
My Osman. Don't be angry at yourself for
this love matter.

161
00:23:57,200 --> 00:24:00,140
It doesn't suit a man.

162
00:24:01,320 --> 00:24:04,540
It's not just about love, Bamsı Bey.

163
00:24:04,540 --> 00:24:11,100
Son, then tell this old man Bamsı Bey what
is bothering you.

164
00:24:23,390 --> 00:24:28,710
Sheikh Edebali is pushing me off.

165
00:24:29,160 --> 00:24:31,760
He doesn't see me worthy of a
conversation.

166
00:24:43,670 --> 00:24:47,850
Son, Sheikh Edebali is a noble one.

167
00:24:48,340 --> 00:24:53,190
Friendship with a noble one is hard. It's
probably for good reason, son.

168
00:24:59,070 --> 00:25:04,490
Keep your eyes open, son. It's not the
time to spread sadness.

169
00:25:05,490 --> 00:25:10,140
Look, a caravan is coming to Kulucahisar
from Nikea.

170
00:25:10,770 --> 00:25:14,050
So they realised that they are trapped.

171
00:25:14,860 --> 00:25:21,360
They did son, they did but, Dündar Bey
ordered Batur for the attack.

172
00:25:21,740 --> 00:25:25,240
It's obvious that he wants to shine
Batur's star.

173
00:25:26,840 --> 00:25:30,840
He's doing the right thing.
He's even late.

174
00:25:31,620 --> 00:25:34,480
Batur will do what's needed eventually.

175
00:25:34,480 --> 00:25:37,920
He needs to know how to stand when he's
up against Alişar.

176
00:25:50,860 --> 00:25:55,540
My Bey. Alişar Bey is back from Konya.

177
00:25:55,840 --> 00:25:58,440
Thank you, Boran.

178
00:25:58,440 --> 00:26:01,810
And my Bey, Edebali...

179
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:06,970
... is settling in Yenipazar with
his friends.

180
00:26:13,530 --> 00:26:17,160
My Bey, now is the right time.

181
00:26:19,740 --> 00:26:22,450
We shall take off.

182
00:26:26,110 --> 00:26:30,310
Keep your eyes on Alişar's mansion. I want
to know who visits him.

183
00:26:30,590 --> 00:26:32,780
Your wish is my command, my Bey.

184
00:26:33,330 --> 00:26:38,490
Bamsı Bey, I'm going to Yenipazar. Keep an
eye on the Tent.

185
00:26:40,130 --> 00:26:42,520
Thank you, my Osman.

186
00:27:30,510 --> 00:27:34,510
What is it Aygül? Did something
block your sun?

187
00:27:35,280 --> 00:27:38,730
Why do you use such dark colours?

188
00:27:40,830 --> 00:27:47,840
Once we take care of our troubles, white
flowers will blossom on our carpets.

189
00:27:48,700 --> 00:27:54,230
Do we cause you trouble, Zöhre?
Just say it.

190
00:27:54,700 --> 00:28:00,750
You're like a splinter, but I'm not
talking about you, Selcan Hatun.

191
00:28:01,070 --> 00:28:02,750
Stay calm.

192
00:28:02,750 --> 00:28:06,540
Then who are you talking about?
Who is causing you trouble?

193
00:28:06,540 --> 00:28:10,940
It's not mine, but everyone's
trouble, Selcan Hatun.

194
00:28:11,110 --> 00:28:15,110
Since Edebali came, we keep
arguing in the Tent.

195
00:28:19,770 --> 00:28:23,050
It's not because a friend came...

196
00:28:23,050 --> 00:28:29,220
... but because you glorify yourself
since your husband became a Bey.

197
00:28:30,900 --> 00:28:40,330
Pity. You're both blind, and you've
forgotten all about our traditions.

198
00:28:41,450 --> 00:28:47,980
Why would his aunt try to arrange
marriage, instead of his uncle?

199
00:28:48,810 --> 00:28:55,050
You went. Seeing how Osman is doing, it
seems like you were denied.

200
00:28:56,180 --> 00:29:00,180
Thant's what happens when you try to
handle things that are not your job.

201
00:29:01,030 --> 00:29:05,980
You say he, I say my son.

202
00:29:05,980 --> 00:29:10,890
If my son wants something from me, I'll
do it no matter what.

203
00:29:11,900 --> 00:29:15,900
That's right. Sheikh Edebali didn't
allow it.

204
00:29:16,270 --> 00:29:19,990
That's right. My Osman is upset.

205
00:29:19,990 --> 00:29:26,380
But, a valiant goes through trouble,
takes shape with love.

206
00:29:27,100 --> 00:29:32,280
I know my valiant. He won't let
go of this.

207
00:29:34,760 --> 00:29:38,990
I'm upset. I'm upset that his father
worked so hard for him.

208
00:29:39,840 --> 00:29:41,810
Why is that?

209
00:29:43,940 --> 00:29:49,010
While Ertuğrul Gazi's son is
chasing ladies...

210
00:29:49,010 --> 00:29:52,980
... my Batur is attacking the
enemy's caravan.

211
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:59,580
They say it for a reason.
A real valiant can be seen in the fields.

212
00:30:48,260 --> 00:30:50,970
You will pay for this!

213
00:30:55,730 --> 00:30:59,870
From now on, swords rule, commander.

214
00:31:01,540 --> 00:31:05,410
We won't stop until you're out
of breath in your castle. Know that.

215
00:31:07,490 --> 00:31:15,860
Now go, tell them Dündar Bey's son Batur
has seized the caravan.

216
00:32:21,970 --> 00:32:26,160
Separate the gold and the
ornaments, Ongun Alp.

217
00:32:26,160 --> 00:32:27,820
Yes, Batur Alp.

218
00:32:27,820 --> 00:32:33,450
Brothers! It's been a long time since we
last attacked an enemy caravan.

219
00:32:33,450 --> 00:32:40,120
From now on, they will fear our wrath!

220
00:32:40,420 --> 00:32:44,260
We will be sudden, like death.

221
00:32:47,890 --> 00:32:52,020
Allahu Akbar!
(Allah is the greatest!)

222
00:32:52,020 --> 00:32:55,890
Long live Dündar Bey!

223
00:33:42,140 --> 00:33:44,350
- Selamın Aleyküm.
- Aleyküm Selam.

224
00:33:44,350 --> 00:33:48,150
What is going on, why is it this crowded?

225
00:33:48,150 --> 00:33:50,990
We're waiting for Sheikh Edebali.

226
00:33:52,490 --> 00:33:54,890
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

227
00:33:55,870 --> 00:33:59,870
My Bey. Now is the time.
Let's go from the back.

228
00:34:01,450 --> 00:34:06,250
You keep an eye out, brother. I'll take
care of the rest.

229
00:34:06,250 --> 00:34:08,200
Yes, my Bey.

230
00:34:27,850 --> 00:34:29,910
Welcome, my Sheikh.

231
00:34:34,750 --> 00:34:37,050
Welcome, my Sheikh.

232
00:34:39,390 --> 00:34:41,890
- Welcome!
- Welcome.

233
00:34:59,580 --> 00:35:01,960
Selamın Aleyküm.
(Peace be unto you)

234
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:06,100
Aleyküm Selam.
(Peace be unto you)

235
00:35:06,910 --> 00:35:09,410
Bismillah.
(In the name of Allah)

236
00:35:28,560 --> 00:35:34,520
Friends, my friends call me "my Sheikh".

237
00:35:35,670 --> 00:35:39,220
My name is Edebali.

238
00:35:39,220 --> 00:35:46,010
We have come here to trade,
taking the example of our prophet.

239
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:54,270
My friends are called Ahis.

240
00:35:55,020 --> 00:35:58,420
Many more of my brothers are on
their ways.

241
00:36:00,940 --> 00:36:02,180
We believe in...

242
00:36:02,690 --> 00:36:06,690
Day of Rising...

243
00:36:08,150 --> 00:36:10,830
which everyone will get their fair shakes.

244
00:36:11,760 --> 00:36:13,960
From now on...

245
00:36:14,430 --> 00:36:17,580
our aim is justice.

246
00:36:20,390 --> 00:36:21,900
We wish that...

247
00:36:22,310 --> 00:36:24,050
the bazaar's order will continue.

248
00:36:24,900 --> 00:36:27,950
We wish that the right one's words ...

249
00:36:28,280 --> 00:36:30,690
will be more important than
the powerful one's.

250
00:36:32,430 --> 00:36:35,350
We wish poor people will be full up.

251
00:36:35,710 --> 00:36:39,180
We wish everyone to help each other.

252
00:36:41,020 --> 00:36:45,020
We wish people to buy cheap goods...

253
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:47,680
and eat them.

254
00:36:48,660 --> 00:36:52,570
We'll support this bazaar from now on.

255
00:36:54,080 --> 00:36:59,260
- May it be good for us.
- Amin.

256
00:37:53,360 --> 00:37:55,390
Welcome, princess. Here.

257
00:38:21,170 --> 00:38:22,760
Princess...

258
00:39:17,560 --> 00:39:22,900
I rolled out the red carpet for
your beautiful eyes.

259
00:39:23,240 --> 00:39:25,450
Welcome to my mansion.

260
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:33,850
Your mansion has a legendary beauty...

261
00:39:34,850 --> 00:39:36,660
Alişar Bey.

262
00:39:37,350 --> 00:39:39,060
It used to be a mansion but...

263
00:39:39,330 --> 00:39:43,800
it became a palace when a
princess like you came.

264
00:39:45,770 --> 00:39:47,860
I did all of this for you.

265
00:39:48,140 --> 00:39:50,880
Roses are the princesses of the flowers.

266
00:39:52,470 --> 00:39:53,740
Here. Come.

267
00:40:05,600 --> 00:40:06,920
My Sheikh...

268
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:13,440
come, Osman Bey.

269
00:40:50,630 --> 00:40:52,640
What do you want from me?

270
00:40:54,010 --> 00:40:55,580
Is it a wish...

271
00:40:56,730 --> 00:40:58,690
or a breath?

272
00:40:59,610 --> 00:41:01,200
A wish.

273
00:41:03,990 --> 00:41:06,200
What if I don't provide it?

274
00:41:12,590 --> 00:41:14,140
Then...

275
00:41:15,980 --> 00:41:17,910
I'll wait.

276
00:41:20,360 --> 00:41:22,210
I'll wait for the time.

277
00:41:25,030 --> 00:41:29,720
Waiting is the ability of
Dervish, Osman Bey.

278
00:41:31,870 --> 00:41:34,190
You'll reach the end of your rope...

279
00:41:35,220 --> 00:41:37,450
your mind will blow up...

280
00:41:38,130 --> 00:41:40,020
and you can't resist it.

281
00:41:42,720 --> 00:41:46,720
Waiting isn't for people...

282
00:41:47,050 --> 00:41:49,470
who are immature.

283
00:41:52,470 --> 00:41:54,060
Waiting...

284
00:41:54,870 --> 00:41:56,880
is the ability of people...

285
00:41:57,540 --> 00:42:00,260
who have self preservation.

286
00:42:02,760 --> 00:42:06,420
You beat people...

287
00:42:07,130 --> 00:42:08,230
but...

288
00:42:09,480 --> 00:42:12,180
this wrestle...

289
00:42:12,890 --> 00:42:15,550
is beyond your depth, Osman Bey.

290
00:42:37,490 --> 00:42:39,420
I wrestled many times.

291
00:42:41,050 --> 00:42:42,670
I fought.

292
00:42:47,250 --> 00:42:48,840
I've never beaten.

293
00:42:54,570 --> 00:42:56,050
But...

294
00:43:01,210 --> 00:43:03,230
Now I have.

295
00:43:09,270 --> 00:43:10,800
Thanks.

296
00:44:24,740 --> 00:44:26,820
My favorite smell.

297
00:44:30,250 --> 00:44:31,760
Jasmine.

298
00:44:38,040 --> 00:44:40,530
It doesn't suit everyone's skin.

299
00:44:50,720 --> 00:44:53,870
You know well about scents, Alişar Bey.

300
00:45:07,220 --> 00:45:08,940
Smell.

301
00:45:13,310 --> 00:45:15,420
Does it suit me?

302
00:45:51,290 --> 00:45:56,650
- What do you want, Sofia?
- We love the same things with you, Alişar Bey.

303
00:45:59,300 --> 00:46:01,810
The smell of the flowers and...

304
00:46:02,170 --> 00:46:03,860
the sound of the gold.

305
00:46:07,740 --> 00:46:09,610
I have both of them.

306
00:46:13,950 --> 00:46:17,950
Do you support Osman and Edebalı or...

307
00:46:20,710 --> 00:46:23,300
the things you love?

308
00:46:32,210 --> 00:46:34,280
What's your problem with Osman?

309
00:46:34,400 --> 00:46:36,240
Tell me.

310
00:46:37,180 --> 00:46:40,300
I care about neither
Osman nor Kayıs.

311
00:46:42,780 --> 00:46:44,850
We were going to
do the thing that Mongols couldn't...

312
00:46:45,110 --> 00:46:48,070
if Osman wasn't around.

313
00:46:51,020 --> 00:46:53,500
We were going to stop Edebalı.

314
00:46:55,250 --> 00:46:57,280
What's your problem with Edebalı?

315
00:46:59,920 --> 00:47:04,280
Edebalı will be a problem for my state...

316
00:47:04,940 --> 00:47:07,560
when he settles here.

317
00:47:08,050 --> 00:47:11,410
Just like he is now, for your state.

318
00:47:25,690 --> 00:47:27,570
Alişar Bey.

319
00:47:33,070 --> 00:47:36,370
I want you to stop Edebalı.

320
00:47:43,800 --> 00:47:47,220
If we join hands, we can hold
the fire and...

321
00:47:49,530 --> 00:47:53,530
rechase it.

322
00:47:56,080 --> 00:47:58,700
Don't let Edebalı...

323
00:47:59,210 --> 00:48:01,540
poison our friendship.

324
00:48:15,920 --> 00:48:18,400
How will I trust you, Sofia?

325
00:48:30,390 --> 00:48:32,040
What is it?

326
00:48:36,800 --> 00:48:38,240
Sir...

327
00:48:38,500 --> 00:48:42,030
Batur, Dündar Bey's son, raided
the Byzantine caravan.

328
00:48:42,110 --> 00:48:45,700
He murdered the soldiers
in the Byzantine lands.

329
00:48:46,610 --> 00:48:48,490
Damn it!

330
00:48:49,190 --> 00:48:52,050
He endangered my lands!

331
00:48:52,620 --> 00:48:54,410
Don't you see it?

332
00:49:03,420 --> 00:49:05,650
You see it, too, Alişar Bey.

333
00:49:07,540 --> 00:49:11,100
Edebalı first poisoned Osman Bey, and now
Dündar Bey.

334
00:49:11,920 --> 00:49:13,220
You...

335
00:49:14,100 --> 00:49:17,130
Do you still think how will you trust me?

336
00:49:19,080 --> 00:49:20,780
I said what's necessary.

337
00:49:23,090 --> 00:49:25,860
If the tax for Mongols decline...

338
00:49:26,850 --> 00:49:29,000
they won't keep you here.

339
00:49:33,360 --> 00:49:36,130
You'll be a shoe sole for
Mongols' shoes...

340
00:49:36,930 --> 00:49:40,040
not Sultan's shadow...

341
00:49:40,390 --> 00:49:41,780
Alişar Bey.

342
00:49:44,740 --> 00:49:46,020
Princsess...

343
00:49:49,250 --> 00:49:53,250
Wait for me tonight. I'll visit you.

344
00:50:57,350 --> 00:50:59,650
Won't you look at me too, Bala?

345
00:51:15,040 --> 00:51:16,710
Allah knows.

346
00:51:17,780 --> 00:51:19,070
You should too.

347
00:51:21,300 --> 00:51:22,860
I promised you.

348
00:51:23,950 --> 00:51:26,020
I'll live for it, Osman.

349
00:51:29,340 --> 00:51:32,400
But, my father's words are above mine.

350
00:51:35,580 --> 00:51:39,210
If he's unwilling, I can't do anything

351
00:51:42,890 --> 00:51:45,730
- Don't come again.
- Bala!

352
00:51:48,310 --> 00:51:49,800
What are you saying?

353
00:51:53,840 --> 00:51:56,490
How will I live without
looking at your...

354
00:51:58,750 --> 00:52:01,170
face and eyes?

355
00:52:05,290 --> 00:52:08,750
I entrusted my heart to you.

356
00:52:11,810 --> 00:52:13,910
I'm here as long as you keep it.

357
00:52:19,310 --> 00:52:23,310
If you give up, I won't resent.

358
00:52:26,810 --> 00:52:28,360
Then...

359
00:52:30,070 --> 00:52:32,090
it's my promise.

360
00:52:34,260 --> 00:52:35,860
You should know that.

361
00:52:37,440 --> 00:52:39,360
Wherever you go...

362
00:52:41,160 --> 00:52:43,330
I'll be behind you.

363
00:52:45,600 --> 00:52:47,240
I promise.

364
00:53:29,580 --> 00:53:33,130
In the 99 names of Allah...

365
00:53:33,130 --> 00:53:36,810
who has the power to create and who
fills our hearts with faith.

366
00:53:37,460 --> 00:53:40,430
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim. (In the name
of Allah, the compassionate, the merciful)

367
00:53:43,820 --> 00:53:47,550
Beys of Kayı, I know...

368
00:53:47,660 --> 00:53:51,660
you're wondering why I've
gathered you here.

369
00:53:52,070 --> 00:53:54,240
I'm not wondering, Dündar Bey.

370
00:53:54,650 --> 00:53:58,690
It's obvious what has happened
in Kulucahisar.

371
00:53:59,050 --> 00:54:00,840
We wear our armours...

372
00:54:00,840 --> 00:54:02,970
and we're waiting for your order.

373
00:54:04,930 --> 00:54:06,960
Samsa Bey is right.

374
00:54:06,960 --> 00:54:08,700
It's time to fight.

375
00:54:08,860 --> 00:54:12,620
Everything's clear now.

376
00:54:12,930 --> 00:54:15,560
Our friends and foes are known.

377
00:54:15,690 --> 00:54:17,930
Sergant Samsa is right.

378
00:54:18,130 --> 00:54:21,570
It's time to fight, Dündar Bey.

379
00:54:22,280 --> 00:54:23,840
Bamsı Bey.

380
00:54:24,880 --> 00:54:26,620
Sergeant Samsa.

381
00:54:26,910 --> 00:54:29,310
I know you're excited.

382
00:54:29,690 --> 00:54:34,780
Now that you want to fight and
you want to loot...

383
00:54:36,260 --> 00:54:39,270
let me show you.

384
00:54:40,310 --> 00:54:41,390
Baturalp!

385
00:54:41,980 --> 00:54:43,270
Bring them.

386
00:55:17,520 --> 00:55:19,730
What are these, Dündar Bey?

387
00:55:20,030 --> 00:55:25,300
Loots that Baturalp gathered
with his own hands.

388
00:55:25,790 --> 00:55:28,820
My brave son showed the world...

389
00:55:28,820 --> 00:55:33,890
how to raid a caravan.

390
00:55:38,550 --> 00:55:40,520
Just like he saved Osman...

391
00:55:41,070 --> 00:55:43,280
he displayed a great valour.

392
00:55:44,900 --> 00:55:48,550
Speaking of him, where is our Osman Bey?

393
00:55:50,170 --> 00:55:53,020
Isn't he invited?

394
00:55:54,120 --> 00:55:56,350
Osman isn't on tent.

395
00:55:56,790 --> 00:55:58,400
He is busy.

396
00:55:59,900 --> 00:56:02,230
Gündüz Bey couldn't tell much.

397
00:56:02,800 --> 00:56:05,840
Osman Bey has a more crucial work.

398
00:56:05,990 --> 00:56:09,820
You know, Selcan Hatun asked for the
girl's hand for Osman but...

399
00:56:09,820 --> 00:56:12,450
Sheikh Edebalı didn't accept.

400
00:56:13,190 --> 00:56:17,190
Osma wants her and Edebalı doesn't accept.

401
00:56:18,430 --> 00:56:20,710
It's none of your business, son.

402
00:56:21,140 --> 00:56:22,900
Why do you say that, Bamsı Bey?

403
00:56:23,960 --> 00:56:27,370
Osman is the son of my uncle...

404
00:56:27,370 --> 00:56:29,130
we carry the same blood.

405
00:56:29,780 --> 00:56:33,190
He wanted her so much...

406
00:56:45,300 --> 00:56:47,660
Master Yannis, do you feel better?

407
00:56:47,790 --> 00:56:51,790
I will if I hear good things from you, my
beautiful Sofia.

408
00:56:51,920 --> 00:56:55,390
Don't worry then.

409
00:56:55,780 --> 00:57:00,590
Alişar Bey's frailties are powerful
enough to make him a puppet.

410
00:57:02,140 --> 00:57:05,110
- Do you know about caravan?
- Yes.

411
00:57:05,820 --> 00:57:09,190
- Kayıs don't stop.
- They shouldn't.

412
00:57:09,710 --> 00:57:13,460
- We'll make use of what they've done.
- How?

413
00:57:13,530 --> 00:57:17,530
Our lovely ally, Alişar Bey...

414
00:57:18,740 --> 00:57:20,350
will do what's necessary.

415
00:57:22,630 --> 00:57:27,340
Then he'll come here. We'll
have dinner together.

416
00:57:27,820 --> 00:57:31,620
But Kalanoz won't like it.

417
00:57:35,970 --> 00:57:38,850
Kalanoz... Fool lover.

418
00:57:40,760 --> 00:57:45,630
Then I'll give the most important
duty to Kalanoz.

419
00:57:47,340 --> 00:57:49,910
He'll kill Edebalı.

420
00:57:50,780 --> 00:57:52,840
Tell him that, Sofia.

421
00:57:53,890 --> 00:57:55,900
Your command, sir.

422
00:57:59,720 --> 00:58:01,110
Salvador.

423
00:58:04,810 --> 00:58:07,410
It's your duty to punish Batur...

424
00:58:07,410 --> 00:58:09,830
who've dared to raid our caravan.

425
00:58:10,850 --> 00:58:14,430
I'll follow that Kayı bandit
like a shadow.

426
00:58:14,620 --> 00:58:18,710
When I'm about to kill him, he'll
be scared.

427
00:58:21,330 --> 00:58:26,680
Now, our matter isn't Osman, who suffers
the pangs of love...

428
00:58:27,850 --> 00:58:31,210
it is my brave son Baturalp...

429
00:58:31,210 --> 00:58:34,430
who is Kayı's hero.

430
00:58:35,420 --> 00:58:38,400
He is the one who raided
unbelievers' caravan and...

431
00:58:38,400 --> 00:58:42,160
who gathered these loots.

432
00:58:42,390 --> 00:58:46,390
As long as I have son like him and...

433
00:58:46,610 --> 00:58:49,450
I have these loots...

434
00:58:49,950 --> 00:58:53,190
no one can put me out.

435
00:58:54,990 --> 00:58:56,950
I can, Dündar Bey.

436
00:59:01,360 --> 00:59:02,950
Alişar Bey.

437
00:59:03,620 --> 00:59:05,080
Yes, Alişar.

438
00:59:07,480 --> 00:59:09,330
Take these!

439
00:59:25,620 --> 00:59:27,670
We gave you a tent...

440
00:59:28,080 --> 00:59:31,230
to be in order..

441
00:59:31,700 --> 00:59:33,730
not to be a bandit!

442
00:59:34,200 --> 00:59:37,430
Since when are you raiding caravans?

443
00:59:37,560 --> 00:59:40,930
These are loots.

444
00:59:41,480 --> 00:59:43,960
Kulucahisar's goods.

445
00:59:46,260 --> 00:59:51,220
How did you forget the treaty
we sealed together, Dündar Bey?

446
00:59:52,140 --> 00:59:55,410
Where are the friendship and alliance?

447
00:59:55,940 --> 00:59:59,130
What will I tell Sofia and Kalanoz?

448
00:59:59,470 --> 01:00:01,990
There's no alliance, Alişar Bey.

449
01:00:02,120 --> 01:00:06,660
They killed our Alps when
you're not around.

450
01:00:11,300 --> 01:00:14,270
I don't care about your Alps.

451
01:00:16,580 --> 01:00:19,540
I care about Seljuqs people.

452
01:00:20,220 --> 01:00:23,260
Did someone let you raid there!

453
01:00:25,400 --> 01:00:29,400
Do we need permission when we
do something to unbelievers?

454
01:00:35,450 --> 01:00:38,430
This tent that you rule...

455
01:00:39,230 --> 01:00:41,890
and manage...

456
01:00:44,910 --> 01:00:49,990
and this tent that you have children in...

457
01:00:50,530 --> 01:00:52,330
belongs to me!

458
01:00:52,350 --> 01:00:55,570
You'll ask everything!

459
01:00:55,570 --> 01:00:58,100
This tent belongs to Süleyman Shah.

460
01:00:58,780 --> 01:01:02,520
It belongs to Kayıs, Alişar Bey!

461
01:01:04,540 --> 01:01:07,440
Don't! Don't.

462
01:01:09,440 --> 01:01:12,410
You can't order me, Batur!

463
01:01:14,270 --> 01:01:16,060
Get out!

464
01:01:40,770 --> 01:01:42,010
Now...

465
01:01:42,290 --> 01:01:45,650
when I brought these loots to Kulucahisar...

466
01:01:46,180 --> 01:01:49,150
and if I see that it lacks even a needle...

467
01:01:50,550 --> 01:01:54,050
I'll kill you with a spear.

468
01:01:54,340 --> 01:01:55,410
A spear!

469
01:02:29,580 --> 01:02:32,020
You summoned me, my princess.

470
01:02:38,050 --> 01:02:40,510
I have a gift for you, Kalanoz.

471
01:02:40,510 --> 01:02:42,980
Your presence is my biggest gift.

472
01:02:43,690 --> 01:02:46,290
Then you'll give me a gift.

473
01:02:46,290 --> 01:02:47,710
What do you want?

474
01:02:52,850 --> 01:02:54,290
Take it.

475
01:02:55,590 --> 01:02:58,440
This sword will accompany your...

476
01:02:58,850 --> 01:03:00,490
heroism.

477
01:03:00,860 --> 01:03:03,100
When the time comes...

478
01:03:04,020 --> 01:03:06,760
I'll marry...

479
01:03:07,490 --> 01:03:09,250
this unique hero.

480
01:03:09,820 --> 01:03:11,890
Nice words are like a song.

481
01:03:13,070 --> 01:03:17,070
But, who do you want me to kill?

482
01:03:24,330 --> 01:03:27,250
A big duty is given to you.

483
01:03:32,400 --> 01:03:35,340
This sword...

484
01:03:36,340 --> 01:03:39,210
will kill Edebalı.

485
01:03:41,930 --> 01:03:44,650
Master Yannis gave the hardest duty...

486
01:03:45,440 --> 01:03:47,820
to the most trustworthy soldier.

487
01:03:49,110 --> 01:03:51,550
I'd do the same.

488
01:03:53,330 --> 01:03:56,150
I'll take this sword as a marriage gift.

489
01:03:57,190 --> 01:04:00,660
I'll rip Edebalı's heart off
and bring it to you.

490
01:04:00,660 --> 01:04:01,680
Then...

491
01:04:03,120 --> 01:04:05,360
we need a good plan...

492
01:04:05,840 --> 01:04:08,220
that no one can prevent.

493
01:04:08,880 --> 01:04:10,660
A good plan.

494
01:04:28,070 --> 01:04:30,740
My Allah. Give me strength!

495
01:04:31,580 --> 01:04:35,580
So that we can cut Alişar's hand and...

496
01:04:35,580 --> 01:04:37,950
give it to him!

497
01:04:39,840 --> 01:04:43,270
My Allah. Give me strength!

498
01:04:50,660 --> 01:04:52,180
Bey.

499
01:04:54,110 --> 01:04:57,440
Bey, Take a breath.

500
01:04:57,720 --> 01:05:00,420
Your uncle doesn't approve it too.

501
01:05:00,420 --> 01:05:03,610
Thank Allah that Osman wasn't here!

502
01:05:04,060 --> 01:05:05,800
Thank Allah that Osman wasn't here!

503
01:05:06,460 --> 01:05:08,410
I hardly stopped myself.

504
01:05:09,130 --> 01:05:10,650
How would we stop him?

505
01:05:12,060 --> 01:05:15,480
You should support Dündar Bey.

506
01:05:15,840 --> 01:05:17,980
He knows what to do.

507
01:05:17,980 --> 01:05:21,980
And then you'll do what's necessary.

508
01:05:22,910 --> 01:05:25,200
It can't be like that, Hatun!

509
01:05:27,890 --> 01:05:29,960
It can't be like that.

510
01:05:31,270 --> 01:05:32,930
The time will come and...

511
01:05:33,760 --> 01:05:36,210
we'll slap Alişar Bey so hard that...

512
01:05:37,390 --> 01:05:39,540
he'll understand why he shouldn't...

513
01:05:41,650 --> 01:05:43,720
show off in Kayı tent.

514
01:05:45,170 --> 01:05:46,740
He'll understand.

515
01:06:18,650 --> 01:06:20,490
Boranalp is coming, my Bey.

516
01:06:37,610 --> 01:06:39,810
- My Bey.
- What is it, Boran?

517
01:06:39,910 --> 01:06:44,110
You were right, Bey. Sofia went to
Alişar Bey's mansion.

518
01:06:47,530 --> 01:06:50,680
- Where is he now?
- He went to the tent..

519
01:06:51,340 --> 01:06:53,650
He raided the tent.

520
01:06:54,180 --> 01:06:55,690
What are you saying, Boran?

521
01:06:55,850 --> 01:06:58,730
He was angry with Dündar Bey for the raid.

522
01:06:58,730 --> 01:07:00,980
What does it have to do with Alişar Bey!

523
01:07:01,060 --> 01:07:03,460
- What did my uncle say?
- My Bey...

524
01:07:03,490 --> 01:07:07,660
Alişar Bey slapped Batur in front of the
Beys, he didn't even say anything.

525
01:07:12,230 --> 01:07:13,630
Alişar Bey...

526
01:07:15,880 --> 01:07:18,040
it's obvious that the castle
plans something.

527
01:07:18,640 --> 01:07:20,970
They want to set on Alişar Bey.

528
01:07:21,850 --> 01:07:23,860
Batur will suffer.

529
01:07:25,000 --> 01:07:28,280
- Where is Batur?
- He got out of the tent.

530
01:07:28,300 --> 01:07:30,380
He went somewhere.

531
01:07:34,260 --> 01:07:36,280
I know where he is.

532
01:07:36,730 --> 01:07:38,840
I hope he won't do anything insane.

533
01:07:41,600 --> 01:07:44,660
- Where are my Alps?
- They're coming.

534
01:07:44,660 --> 01:07:48,390
- Come to Şahin Hill.
- Your command, my Bey.

535
01:08:17,400 --> 01:08:19,160
Dündar Bey!

536
01:08:20,830 --> 01:08:22,570
Are the things I heard true?

537
01:08:23,240 --> 01:08:26,630
Alişar Bey questioned all of you.

538
01:08:26,630 --> 01:08:30,040
He slapped my Batur, and you
didn't say anything.

539
01:08:30,130 --> 01:08:33,920
Keep your nose out of men's business!

540
01:08:34,030 --> 01:08:38,820
I wouldn't approve that slap!

541
01:08:39,160 --> 01:08:43,160
No one can slap Kayı's brave man!

542
01:08:43,380 --> 01:08:47,130
- How can you...
- How can I remain silent, right!

543
01:08:48,120 --> 01:08:53,230
He is the Banner lord, Hatun! Banner lord!

544
01:08:53,270 --> 01:08:56,370
What will we do if he tell us to leave?

545
01:08:56,840 --> 01:08:59,870
We can't go back!

546
01:08:59,960 --> 01:09:03,310
There are Byzantine and Mongol beyond!

547
01:09:04,610 --> 01:09:08,610
Don't you see that we're trying
to get organized?

548
01:09:12,400 --> 01:09:16,030
After all...

549
01:09:16,410 --> 01:09:19,770
Alişar Bey is...

550
01:09:19,960 --> 01:09:23,090
Batur's brother is law.

551
01:09:25,610 --> 01:09:27,440
He won't take it as a matter of pride!

552
01:09:27,730 --> 01:09:30,190
He'll bear it.

553
01:09:30,520 --> 01:09:32,410
He'll bear it!

554
01:09:32,960 --> 01:09:35,400
It's a must.

555
01:09:35,940 --> 01:09:39,940
I'm sure that...

556
01:09:41,020 --> 01:09:42,730
he'll pay the price for that slap.

557
01:09:44,010 --> 01:09:46,520
But...

558
01:09:46,880 --> 01:09:49,200
we should do what's necessary now.

559
01:11:31,180 --> 01:11:33,520
My dear Batur's mother...

560
01:11:33,810 --> 01:11:35,130
What happened?

561
01:11:35,930 --> 01:11:37,440
Pull yourself together.

562
01:11:39,830 --> 01:11:43,290
How can Alişar Bey do something like
that, Selcan Hatun?

563
01:11:46,450 --> 01:11:49,260
My son, my Batur...

564
01:11:50,120 --> 01:11:52,340
Allah knows where he is.

565
01:11:52,850 --> 01:11:54,310
How he is.

566
01:11:55,870 --> 01:12:01,240
Alişar Bey slapped
Batur, apparently, but...

567
01:12:01,700 --> 01:12:06,550
Alişar Bey will regret it.

568
01:12:08,150 --> 01:12:13,540
However, I am concerned about Batur,
Zöhre.

569
01:12:13,650 --> 01:12:19,100
You know him very well.
He is from your blood.

570
01:12:19,130 --> 01:12:22,460
Tell me.
Would he do something crazy?

571
01:12:22,460 --> 01:12:28,960
If it is being about man, each one of
our man is the same, Selcan Hatun.

572
01:12:29,320 --> 01:12:32,370
He doesn't hurt himself, in sha Allah.

573
01:12:32,370 --> 01:12:37,840
He doesn't make me worry, in sha Allah.

574
01:12:40,910 --> 01:12:44,680
Come on. Pull yourself together.

575
01:12:45,180 --> 01:12:49,720
We need to stand.
You need to stand.

576
01:12:49,760 --> 01:12:54,090
You need to pray and stand.

577
01:12:56,020 --> 01:13:00,230
You meet your son as soon as possible,
in sha Allah.

578
01:13:00,320 --> 01:13:01,690
In sha Allah.

579
01:13:01,880 --> 01:13:05,980
May you relieve as soon as possible.

580
01:13:06,730 --> 01:13:10,820
And the unity of our tent continues,
in sha Allah.

581
01:13:11,220 --> 01:13:12,860
In sha Allah.

582
01:14:05,410 --> 01:14:07,540
Efendis!
(Gentlemen!)

583
01:14:07,600 --> 01:14:09,250
Alişar Bey.

584
01:14:16,820 --> 01:14:22,800
Don't you respect the Banner lord
of Seljuq?

585
01:14:23,200 --> 01:14:27,100
Even in my lands, in my bazaar.

586
01:14:27,140 --> 01:14:29,770
What a tactlessness?

587
01:14:43,500 --> 01:14:45,900
Sit, Alişar Bey.

588
01:14:50,210 --> 01:14:58,810
In Baghdad Cemetery, Behlül dug
a grave and fell asleep in it.

589
01:14:58,890 --> 01:15:05,030
Sultan Reşit ordered to find him
immediately.

590
01:15:05,030 --> 01:15:09,390
Soldiers started to search for Behlül.

591
01:15:09,390 --> 01:15:12,040
They finally found him.

592
01:15:12,070 --> 01:15:17,840
They woke that poor up by poking him
with their spears.

593
01:15:18,710 --> 01:15:25,470
You know, it's Behlül.
He closed his eyes and opened his mouth.

594
01:15:25,680 --> 01:15:28,890
Asked: "why did you wake me up?"

595
01:15:29,550 --> 01:15:37,630
Soldiers took him to Sultan at once.

596
01:15:39,170 --> 01:15:43,100
While smiling, Sultan asked...

597
01:15:44,050 --> 01:15:48,950
"You argued with soldiers for waking you
up"

598
01:15:49,700 --> 01:15:51,920
What is the reason?

599
01:15:51,920 --> 01:15:56,660
Behlül started talking.

600
01:15:56,730 --> 01:16:01,620
He said he was a Sultan in his dream.

601
01:16:01,620 --> 01:16:09,440
He said he had soldiers,
a palace, servants.

602
01:16:10,310 --> 01:16:15,010
Everything was ruined when
they woke me up.

603
01:16:15,010 --> 01:16:18,550
Sultan Reşit laughed.

604
01:16:18,550 --> 01:16:26,110
He said it was just a dream.

605
01:16:27,360 --> 01:16:34,500
Behlül looked at Sultan,
then the soldiers.

606
01:16:36,510 --> 01:16:39,860
And he said, "Then, tell me, Sultan."

607
01:16:40,170 --> 01:16:48,410
"What is the difference between my reign
in the dream and your reign here?"

608
01:16:51,330 --> 01:16:59,900
He said, "Mine has ended when I woke up,
yours will end when you die."

609
01:17:04,440 --> 01:17:06,260
Then...

610
01:17:08,390 --> 01:17:11,730
Tell us, Alişar Bey.

611
01:17:12,540 --> 01:17:22,310
You rely on your soldiers and power, so
you try to question us.

612
01:17:23,030 --> 01:17:28,360
Is it worth a Sultanate which will end
someday?

613
01:17:29,880 --> 01:17:32,410
Think about it...

614
01:17:33,510 --> 01:17:39,690
Is that tactless you, who comes in
without permission and wait for respect...

615
01:17:39,760 --> 01:17:47,070
or is it us who ignored a mortal?

616
01:18:03,690 --> 01:18:10,990
I came here to question you about coming
here without my permission.

617
01:18:13,040 --> 01:18:18,370
However, I see that I will be pleased to
have you here.

618
01:18:18,960 --> 01:18:21,010
Forgive me, my Sheik.

619
01:18:26,790 --> 01:18:31,550
Alişar Bey, you know that...

620
01:18:31,590 --> 01:18:36,230
in that raid, my friends have been
martyred.

621
01:18:37,410 --> 01:18:42,280
My Ahi brothers died here.

622
01:18:42,760 --> 01:18:46,210
Now it is also our land.

623
01:18:49,170 --> 01:18:53,820
We know Ahi order and Ahi tradition.

624
01:18:54,010 --> 01:18:59,610
Your essence gives us power and makes our
bazaar mighty.

625
01:19:00,060 --> 01:19:11,010
brought to you by kurulusosman.online

626
01:19:35,570 --> 01:19:38,930
You can't order me!

627
01:19:42,710 --> 01:19:46,740
I'll take revenge, Alişar!

628
01:19:47,040 --> 01:19:50,310
You disgraced me in front of my Beys!

629
01:19:53,210 --> 01:19:58,370
Onur Alp! Sercan Alp!
Leave me alone! Don't come!

630
01:20:13,800 --> 01:20:15,470
You heh!

631
01:20:15,500 --> 01:20:18,610
I'll not leave you alone here.

632
01:20:18,770 --> 01:20:21,220
Let's finish our thing.

633
01:20:21,670 --> 01:20:23,820
Attack.

634
01:20:46,950 --> 01:20:49,060
Hold on brother!

635
01:20:55,940 --> 01:20:57,920
My brother!

636
01:20:57,970 --> 01:21:00,500
Osman... Attack!

637
01:21:21,900 --> 01:21:24,760
- Brother.
- Eyvallah (thank you) brother.

638
01:21:31,720 --> 01:21:34,210
Kill them already!

639
01:21:34,210 --> 01:21:36,520
Allah is eternal!

640
01:22:04,200 --> 01:22:06,630
Losers!

641
01:22:15,220 --> 01:22:17,680
It's nice to see you, Osman.

642
01:22:25,020 --> 01:22:27,860
I'll take revenge for Juan.

643
01:22:31,130 --> 01:22:33,680
Leave him to me, brother.

644
01:22:34,310 --> 01:22:38,050
Not only Juan, but we
also killed all your dogs!

645
01:22:38,050 --> 01:22:41,320
Now, it's your time.

646
01:22:42,180 --> 01:22:44,260
Die!

647
01:23:24,720 --> 01:23:29,480
- Batur Bey, are you okay?
- I am fine, Abdurrahman Ghazi.

648
01:23:37,910 --> 01:23:41,160
Then, we can watch the show.

649
01:23:44,180 --> 01:23:46,220
Leave a bit to us.

650
01:23:46,230 --> 01:23:49,400
We won't get any, brother.

651
01:24:13,630 --> 01:24:18,720
- Are you fine, brother?
- Yes, brother. I am alive thanks to you.

652
01:24:18,800 --> 01:24:24,000
You are my brother.
I'd do anything for you.

653
01:24:24,000 --> 01:24:26,450
Eyvallah, my brother.
(Thank you.)

654
01:24:34,210 --> 01:24:36,160
- Boran.
- Yes, my Bey?

655
01:24:36,160 --> 01:24:41,020
Take Batur to the tent with Boğaç and
Erkut.

656
01:24:41,560 --> 01:24:46,290
Let Bamsı Bey know that we have
Aybars' murderer.

657
01:24:47,570 --> 01:24:49,640
Eyvallah (okay) my Bey.

658
01:24:51,910 --> 01:24:54,320
What are we going to do with this dog,
Osman Bey?

659
01:24:58,210 --> 01:25:01,060
We will take him to the cave.

660
01:25:01,550 --> 01:25:04,720
He'll tell us about his owners.

661
01:25:29,530 --> 01:25:33,570
My Bey. I don't understand.

662
01:25:33,570 --> 01:25:36,450
We went there angrily and we are returning
calmly now.

663
01:25:37,470 --> 01:25:41,050
Where did I come from, Nizamettin?

664
01:25:41,400 --> 01:25:46,420
- Konya, my Bey.
- Hah, at least you know that.

665
01:25:46,440 --> 01:25:48,860
I'll tell you what you don't know.

666
01:25:49,550 --> 01:25:52,610
Konya is not in good condition.

667
01:25:53,660 --> 01:25:58,430
I am here to represent Sultan, but...

668
01:25:58,460 --> 01:26:04,540
I saw in Konya that there is no Sultan
to represent.

669
01:26:05,820 --> 01:26:09,910
Mongols occupied there.

670
01:26:10,930 --> 01:26:14,450
Then, what should we do, Nizamettin?

671
01:26:15,500 --> 01:26:18,540
You know the best, my Bey.

672
01:26:19,250 --> 01:26:23,070
The best thing to do is to be the Sultan.

673
01:26:24,720 --> 01:26:32,560
Being Sultan requires money,
money requires good craftsmen.

674
01:26:33,730 --> 01:26:38,780
Now, tell me. Is there any better
craftsman better than Ahis...

675
01:26:38,810 --> 01:26:42,160
in this country?

676
01:26:43,080 --> 01:26:45,000
No, my Bey.

677
01:26:45,140 --> 01:26:50,730
Then, we know what we have to do.
Edebalı will produce and sell...

678
01:26:50,870 --> 01:26:55,060
and Alişar Bey will gain money.

679
01:26:59,420 --> 01:27:02,320
You shall please them.

680
01:27:40,470 --> 01:27:43,160
Who is this young one, Nizamettin?

681
01:27:44,050 --> 01:27:47,540
She is Sheik Edebalı's daughter
Bala Hatun, my Bey.

682
01:27:53,940 --> 01:27:55,830
Bala.

683
01:28:22,710 --> 01:28:24,740
Enough.

684
01:28:25,750 --> 01:28:27,820
Wait.

685
01:28:34,040 --> 01:28:36,760
They can hold their breath a long time.

686
01:28:36,860 --> 01:28:39,680
Let's try this.

687
01:28:44,420 --> 01:28:46,660
There is no easy way to die for you!

688
01:29:34,110 --> 01:29:39,170
Is this the head of my son's murderers,
my Osman?

689
01:29:39,170 --> 01:29:41,150
Yes, Bamsı Bey.

690
01:30:17,130 --> 01:30:19,130
My Osman.

691
01:30:40,910 --> 01:30:42,660
Tell me.

692
01:30:44,850 --> 01:30:47,390
Tell me, infidel.

693
01:30:49,570 --> 01:30:54,340
Did you give my Aybar's death order with
this tongue?

694
01:30:58,040 --> 01:31:04,710
Tell me, infidel!
Do you hear your allies with this ear?

695
01:31:09,670 --> 01:31:13,150
Do you see with this eye?

696
01:31:16,100 --> 01:31:20,480
Did you kill my Demirbüken with this hand?

697
01:31:22,870 --> 01:31:26,570
Speak, infidel!
Speak!

698
01:31:29,460 --> 01:31:31,630
How can you...

699
01:31:32,760 --> 01:31:37,030
be so dishonored?

700
01:31:46,230 --> 01:31:51,680
My Osman! My Osman, are you done
with him?

701
01:31:51,680 --> 01:31:54,350
I'll give him to you when I'm done,
Bamsı Bey.

702
01:31:56,670 --> 01:32:00,970
Give him to me when you are done,
my Osman.

703
01:32:32,220 --> 01:32:39,470
Edebalı's Ahis will bring benefit to our
bazaar. What a smart move, my Bey.

704
01:32:43,640 --> 01:32:50,730
Not only Bazaar. Edebalı will bring
benefit to my house too.

705
01:32:54,520 --> 01:32:57,860
What's in your mind, my Bey?

706
01:32:58,570 --> 01:33:01,100
She is nice.

707
01:33:03,480 --> 01:33:06,370
I liked Bala Hatun quite a lot.

708
01:33:06,770 --> 01:33:11,990
I witness how beautiful creatures Allah
creates.

709
01:33:12,250 --> 01:33:19,620
And this gazelle comes across with a
hunter like me.

710
01:33:21,000 --> 01:33:25,910
But, my Bey, your marriage with
Aygül Hatun is near.

711
01:33:26,320 --> 01:33:30,390
- Do you give her up?
- Why would I?

712
01:33:30,820 --> 01:33:32,980
I am Alişar Bey.

713
01:33:34,110 --> 01:33:37,270
I have room for everyone.

714
01:33:37,320 --> 01:33:42,010
Bey's daughter in a room, Sheik's
daughter in another room.

715
01:33:44,430 --> 01:33:46,880
Isn't this better?

716
01:33:47,350 --> 01:33:51,800
Masha Allah, you are like a lion,
my Bey.

717
01:33:51,800 --> 01:33:56,630
But I don't think both Edebalı and Dündar
Bey would accept this.

718
01:33:57,030 --> 01:34:02,220
If they don't, Dündar Bey's daughter is
not important.

719
01:34:03,580 --> 01:34:12,490
My mansion needs someone like Bala Hatun
who is beautiful, diligent and nimble.

720
01:34:16,090 --> 01:34:18,240
Let's wait.

721
01:34:19,620 --> 01:34:22,100
Everything has a time.

722
01:34:45,110 --> 01:34:48,160
Enough.
Please, stop.

723
01:34:50,760 --> 01:34:53,220
- Tell us!
- Please...

724
01:35:08,120 --> 01:35:11,080
My death won't be good for you.

725
01:35:11,550 --> 01:35:15,300
I know a lot.
I'll speak.

726
01:35:17,350 --> 01:35:21,680
I'll help you save Edebalı if you
forgive me!

727
01:35:26,710 --> 01:35:31,640
Tell me!
Is Edebalı in danger?

728
01:35:33,400 --> 01:35:36,130
I'll tell you if you let me live.

729
01:35:39,310 --> 01:35:41,520
I will.

730
01:35:42,080 --> 01:35:44,110
Tell me.

731
01:35:46,560 --> 01:35:48,800
Tell me!

732
01:35:50,340 --> 01:35:53,670
Tonight, Edebalı...

733
01:35:55,010 --> 01:35:57,740
What will happen to Edebalı tonight?

734
01:35:58,950 --> 01:36:03,650
Kalanoz will kill Edebalı with his men.

735
01:36:09,010 --> 01:36:14,090
Look at me, if you are playing,
you will beg to die...

736
01:36:14,330 --> 01:36:16,310
instead of begging to live!

737
01:36:16,310 --> 01:36:21,120
- You'll let me live, right?
- I will...

738
01:36:25,300 --> 01:36:29,950
But, I don't know about Bamsı Bey.

739
01:36:33,420 --> 01:36:36,150
Don't give me to him.

740
01:36:36,280 --> 01:36:38,540
Please, Osman Bey.

741
01:36:39,440 --> 01:36:41,640
Don't give me to him.

742
01:36:41,700 --> 01:36:45,200
If this infidel is right, it's hard to get
there on time.

743
01:36:45,230 --> 01:36:49,840
It's pitch-black outside. Horses are tired.
It will be hard to get there, Osman Bey.

744
01:36:50,970 --> 01:36:53,080
- May Khidr be with us
- Amin.

745
01:36:53,090 --> 01:36:55,050
Let's go there at once.

746
01:37:01,880 --> 01:37:03,900
Go, valiant.

747
01:37:27,610 --> 01:37:30,820
It's a flawless table, Princess.

748
01:37:31,200 --> 01:37:33,530
Your guest will like it.

749
01:37:33,530 --> 01:37:40,660
Everything in this castle is to satisfy
us, Helen.

750
01:37:43,590 --> 01:37:48,500
Come here, Bannerlord Alişar Bey.

751
01:37:48,510 --> 01:37:52,210
Come and tell us what you are going to
do for us.

752
01:38:05,120 --> 01:38:08,130
Princess Sofia is waiting for you,
Alişar Bey.

753
01:38:08,670 --> 01:38:12,580
- Get well soon, Commander.
- Thank you, Alişar Bey.

754
01:38:12,600 --> 01:38:18,280
We'd get injured in battlefield back then,
now we do while defending our caravan.

755
01:38:32,900 --> 01:38:35,250
Welcome, Alişar Bey.

756
01:38:37,550 --> 01:38:40,170
Thank you, Princess.

757
01:38:42,030 --> 01:38:45,600
I brought Dündar Bey and Batur into line.

758
01:38:46,310 --> 01:38:50,820
In front of every Kayı Beys.

759
01:38:51,350 --> 01:38:56,570
The goods that you lost during the attack
have been brought to your castle.

760
01:38:57,100 --> 01:39:02,270
From now on, I take precautions to
not let something like that happen.

761
01:39:02,910 --> 01:39:04,610
Don't worry.

762
01:39:05,200 --> 01:39:11,430
I have never doubted that you'd do
what is necessary, Alişar Bey.

763
01:39:24,230 --> 01:39:31,710
Here is my gift, Princess.

764
01:39:34,410 --> 01:39:36,530
You are very kind.

765
01:39:59,780 --> 01:40:03,430
It's nothing in the light of your
beauty, but...

766
01:40:03,510 --> 01:40:09,880
you will make me happy if you wear
this as a symbol of our friendship.

767
01:40:35,010 --> 01:40:37,870
What a right choice.

768
01:40:43,030 --> 01:40:45,480
Like all of your other choices.

769
01:40:48,550 --> 01:40:50,570
Here.

770
01:41:12,720 --> 01:41:16,250
I prepared sherbet for you.

771
01:41:16,820 --> 01:41:19,100
I hope you like it.

772
01:41:36,040 --> 01:41:39,910
Your table represents you, Princess.

773
01:41:40,370 --> 01:41:43,180
Flawless.

774
01:41:50,620 --> 01:41:53,630
I am embarrassed about what happened.

775
01:41:53,790 --> 01:41:58,720
You did your best to meet the harm,
Alişar Bey.

776
01:41:58,720 --> 01:42:01,660
You don't need to be embarrassed.

777
01:42:02,190 --> 01:42:09,820
A simple caravan is not important while
there is our allied power...

778
01:42:10,100 --> 01:42:14,490
that we'll use from now on.

779
01:42:40,820 --> 01:42:44,890
- The day has come, finally.
- Where are the wardens, Nizamettin?

780
01:42:45,150 --> 01:42:49,230
I called them here. They'll be here soon.
Take care of them.

781
01:42:49,230 --> 01:42:52,530
- What about Edebalı's house?
- The stone house in the other street.

782
01:42:52,620 --> 01:42:57,720
When you kill wardens, the bazaar will
be defenseless. Edebalı is easy.

783
01:42:58,610 --> 01:43:02,200
His daughters Bala and Gonca are home.
And two dervishes of his.

784
01:43:02,230 --> 01:43:05,760
One of them is the one who introduced
himself as father Marcus.

785
01:43:06,190 --> 01:43:10,910
Nizamettin.
This is going to end tonight.

786
01:43:11,250 --> 01:43:15,580
If something goes wrong, you'll
be responsible.

787
01:43:17,670 --> 01:43:21,980
There will be nothing wrong, Commander
Kalanoz. Be sure about this.

788
01:43:22,770 --> 01:43:26,090
They will perform ablution first.

789
01:43:28,160 --> 01:43:30,860
They read Quran before going to bed.

790
01:44:12,280 --> 01:44:14,230
They'll sleep and close the doors.

791
01:44:14,780 --> 01:44:18,200
They think that the Devil
can't open the doors.

792
01:49:05,970 --> 01:49:07,350
Osman.

793
01:49:18,050 --> 01:49:20,310
How did you know we were coming?

794
01:49:20,780 --> 01:49:23,460
Salvador, dog of Yannis, whispered to me.

795
01:49:24,400 --> 01:49:27,740
Now he's trying to persuade
Bamsı Bey to keep his head!

796
01:49:28,210 --> 01:49:32,440
I can still feel the warmth of
the wounds we opened in you.

797
01:49:32,480 --> 01:49:37,120
Just wait, Kalonos, you will burn
in the wounds you opened.

798
01:49:51,460 --> 01:49:54,950
Those who come unnoticed,
sleep without a bed, don't you know?

799
01:50:14,710 --> 01:50:16,540
Seeds of the infidels!

800
01:50:41,490 --> 01:50:43,170
Do it, Osman.

801
01:50:43,610 --> 01:50:44,650
Do it!

802
01:50:45,510 --> 01:50:48,350
I told you, you will
burn in those wounds.

803
01:51:31,690 --> 01:51:33,550
This is for Demirbüken!

804
01:51:40,560 --> 01:51:42,270
And this is for Kanturalı!

805
01:52:12,960 --> 01:52:14,170
Osman!

806
01:52:26,010 --> 01:52:28,330
It has just begun, Osman.

807
01:52:29,280 --> 01:52:31,340
I'm in no rush.

808
01:52:31,980 --> 01:52:38,860
I will first deal with Sofia, then
with the dog that's her father.

809
01:52:40,490 --> 01:52:46,390
You... You are not strong enough, Osman.

810
01:52:47,770 --> 01:52:52,500
You are nothing compared to us.

811
01:52:59,850 --> 01:53:02,690
Until I ride the horse of
doom and wreck Kulucahisar...

812
01:53:03,550 --> 01:53:06,290
... until I spill the poison
out of Sofia's teeth...

813
01:53:07,450 --> 01:53:11,450
... and stab Yannis in the
monastery he came from...

814
01:53:12,040 --> 01:53:14,130
... dying is forbidden to me!

815
01:54:07,270 --> 01:54:08,700
My Aybars...

816
01:54:10,750 --> 01:54:13,210
... never liked weapons.

817
01:54:14,220 --> 01:54:21,340
He told me in his childhood, "You can take
weapons father, I'll pick up the pencil."

818
01:54:25,590 --> 01:54:33,580
Back then, I had muscles like the breast
of a buffalo, and chest like a stallion.

819
01:54:33,600 --> 01:54:36,290
I was strong, I was strong.

820
01:54:39,040 --> 01:54:45,990
Other Beys would send their children
to test their skills at weapons...

821
01:54:46,280 --> 01:54:50,940
... but Aybars would just
say "I don't want weapons."

822
01:54:55,880 --> 01:54:57,840
They told me then...

823
01:54:58,990 --> 01:55:04,210
..." countries are taken with weapons,
but held with a pencil.

824
01:55:05,210 --> 01:55:12,220
I said "Okay. I will keep my weapon,
you can keep your pencil, son."

825
01:55:16,450 --> 01:55:22,880
But, you infidels just
couldn't allow that, could you?

826
01:55:25,240 --> 01:55:28,340
They started harassing my
Aybars from his childhood.

827
01:55:29,330 --> 01:55:31,850
They didn't let him study!

828
01:55:32,730 --> 01:55:36,730
After deciding there was no other way...

829
01:55:37,630 --> 01:55:42,310
... he mounted his horse, and
took his weapon on his hand.

830
01:55:48,230 --> 01:55:51,230
My son was a valiant warrior.

831
01:55:51,750 --> 01:55:54,260
He sided with my Osman...

832
01:55:55,290 --> 01:55:58,260
... and they became a mountain together.

833
01:56:00,820 --> 01:56:01,780
Once...

834
01:56:03,790 --> 01:56:05,910
... my Aybars stood
in front of me.

835
01:56:06,510 --> 01:56:11,090
He said, "Father.". I said,
"Tell me, my brave son!"

836
01:56:12,390 --> 01:56:13,970
He said, "Father."

837
01:56:14,900 --> 01:56:17,010
" I have a request."

838
01:56:20,320 --> 01:56:22,510
I said, " You can wish
anything, my son!"

839
01:56:24,050 --> 01:56:29,240
I said "Your father would
make far places close...

840
01:56:29,340 --> 01:56:31,770
... and make impossible
things possible for you."

841
01:56:32,340 --> 01:56:33,420
I said...

842
01:56:34,560 --> 01:56:41,900
" If you want, your father would spit
fire, and melt mountains of iron for you!"

843
01:56:44,130 --> 01:56:45,810
"I'm in love." ...

844
01:56:48,000 --> 01:56:48,750
...he said.

845
01:56:51,280 --> 01:56:52,640
"I'm in love."

846
01:56:58,110 --> 01:57:00,840
My heart was like an erupting volcano.

847
01:57:01,130 --> 01:57:04,750
"Okay!" I said. "Okay! It's tradition!"

848
01:57:05,660 --> 01:57:08,060
The lover will take the one he loves.

849
01:57:53,750 --> 01:57:55,790
It's me, Tursun Efendi.

850
01:57:57,220 --> 01:57:58,870
Listen to me, Tursun Fakı.

851
01:57:58,880 --> 01:58:02,880
What are you doing, Osman Bey, are you
trying to get what you need like this?

852
01:58:03,010 --> 01:58:07,840
It's not about me, Tursun Fakı,
everyone's lives are in danger.

853
01:58:27,030 --> 01:58:28,280
My Sheikh!

854
01:58:54,870 --> 01:58:59,150
First, you made our store a marketplace.

855
01:59:00,590 --> 01:59:04,140
Then you became an armour for our death.

856
01:59:05,710 --> 01:59:09,260
Now, I ask you again, Osman Bey.

857
01:59:10,360 --> 01:59:11,950
Is it a wish...

858
01:59:12,790 --> 01:59:15,040
... or a breath?

859
01:59:17,690 --> 01:59:20,150
I said "Would Sheikh Edebali...

860
01:59:21,750 --> 01:59:23,370
... accept me in...

861
01:59:25,410 --> 01:59:30,390
... If I weep blood from
my eyes, and rip my chest?

862
01:59:32,410 --> 01:59:36,410
- And did I?
- You didn't.

863
01:59:39,560 --> 01:59:41,030
"If I, like Eyüp (Prophet)...

864
01:59:42,120 --> 01:59:44,620
... was attacked by wolves...

865
01:59:45,400 --> 01:59:50,130
... weep blood, like Yahya (Prophet)...

866
01:59:51,120 --> 01:59:52,570
... prayed on Mount Tur...

867
01:59:54,010 --> 01:59:56,530
... like Musa (Prophet)...

868
01:59:57,260 --> 02:00:02,870
... would Sheikh Edebali accept me in?"
I said.

869
02:00:04,120 --> 02:00:07,850
- Did I?
- You didn't.

870
02:00:10,220 --> 02:00:14,080
"If I be a fish like Yunus...

871
02:00:15,340 --> 02:00:19,900
... stay in a well for days, like Yusuf...

872
02:00:21,650 --> 02:00:26,670
... weep blood for Yusuf, like Yakup...

873
02:00:28,770 --> 02:00:33,730
... would Sheikh Edebali accept me in?"
I said.

874
02:00:34,490 --> 02:00:37,870
- Did I?
- You didn't.

875
02:00:39,180 --> 02:00:45,110
I'm embarrassed and ashamed for
eternity, Sheikh Edebali.

876
02:00:46,900 --> 02:00:54,480
Now I can finally say it. My only wish is
your blessed breath.

877
02:00:56,530 --> 02:00:58,950
Your one prayer.

878
02:01:04,540 --> 02:01:10,330
There are Abdalans, who come to us,
dispersed by love.

879
02:01:11,550 --> 02:01:17,540
There are Bacıyans, who think of serving
us as their duties.

880
02:01:18,200 --> 02:01:29,070
But, your only purpose should be holy
war, in the name of Allah.

881
02:01:30,820 --> 02:01:35,850
As long as you fight this holy war...

882
02:01:36,430 --> 02:01:39,090
... our breaths will be with you, son.

883
02:01:40,430 --> 02:01:43,430
Thank you, Sheikh Edebali.

884
02:01:44,810 --> 02:01:49,840
Your purpose is to prevent Oğuz
Clans oppression...

885
02:01:50,440 --> 02:01:53,140
... in the name of Allah.

886
02:01:53,290 --> 02:01:57,290
You shall be one of Gaziyans, with
this purpose.

887
02:01:58,360 --> 02:02:06,020
A man doesn't put responsibilities behind
for love, for passion.

888
02:02:07,500 --> 02:02:11,500
Being the ruler of Gaziyans will
suit you better.

889
02:02:12,210 --> 02:02:17,070
My father described you as Oğuz's light.

890
02:02:18,460 --> 02:02:26,140
Even if it costs us our lives, we won't
let this light go off.

891
02:02:28,670 --> 02:02:35,700
As Allah tested Adam with getting
close to the tree...

892
02:02:36,170 --> 02:02:41,160
... Allah tests Adam's children with...

893
02:02:41,160 --> 02:02:44,770
... patience and gratitude under every
circumstance, Osman Bey.

894
02:02:46,850 --> 02:02:52,430
Because in the world of reason, whatever
happens to a person...

895
02:02:52,430 --> 02:02:56,840
... happens for a hidden reason.

896
02:02:57,820 --> 02:03:00,350
With patience and gratitude...

897
02:03:01,550 --> 02:03:03,790
... under your mighty shadow...

898
02:03:05,040 --> 02:03:07,960
... we could take shape.

899
02:03:10,160 --> 02:03:12,430
Thank you for that.

900
02:04:02,900 --> 02:04:07,470
He has begun taking shape on your
door, my Sheikh.

901
02:04:31,290 --> 02:04:33,120
Osman Bey.

902
02:04:34,430 --> 02:04:36,660
Bala Hatun.

903
02:04:37,840 --> 02:04:43,060
Sheikh Edebali's breath and prayers are
with us, thankfully.

904
02:04:43,720 --> 02:04:45,100
Thankfully.

905
02:04:46,710 --> 02:04:51,550
It's patience from now on. We shall
patiently wait for your father to call us.

906
02:04:52,840 --> 02:04:56,840
To wait, we have both hearts...

907
02:04:58,240 --> 02:05:00,170
... and love.

908
02:05:03,270 --> 02:05:07,400
- Now if you excuse me.
- Of course, Osman Bey.

909
02:05:07,400 --> 02:05:09,760
May Allah guide your way.

910
02:05:49,750 --> 02:05:55,900
Fire everywhere, poisonous snakes
everywhere.

911
02:05:56,770 --> 02:06:00,960
Where does Batur go unannounced like this?

912
02:06:02,550 --> 02:06:06,100
His pride was injured in front of
everyone.

913
02:06:06,100 --> 02:06:09,180
You embarrassed him!

914
02:06:10,110 --> 02:06:14,940
It was his uncle who hit him.
Not a stranger!

915
02:06:15,150 --> 02:06:18,310
If you don't say anything, he'll do
it again.

916
02:06:18,310 --> 02:06:22,230
My Batur didn't say anything wrong.
Why would that coward hit him?

917
02:06:22,650 --> 02:06:31,790
Kayı Bey's son gets slapped by a fancy Banner
Lord who puts cinnamon juice on his beard.

918
02:06:32,390 --> 02:06:35,770
My Allah, protect us.

919
02:06:35,770 --> 02:06:37,780
May I come in, Dündar Bey?

920
02:06:38,170 --> 02:06:40,260
Come in, Boran Alp.

921
02:06:48,080 --> 02:06:52,480
Batur! My Batur, my valiant what
happened to you?

922
02:06:53,250 --> 02:06:57,250
Batur! My son.

923
02:07:00,100 --> 02:07:02,320
I was ambushed in the woods.

924
02:07:04,100 --> 02:07:06,670
Osman saved my life.

925
02:07:35,570 --> 02:07:37,580
Master Yannis.

926
02:07:39,150 --> 02:07:42,670
- Kalonoz.
- What happened?

927
02:07:42,670 --> 02:07:45,090
We found his corpse in front
of the castle, sir.

928
02:07:45,090 --> 02:07:47,370
Useless fool!

929
02:07:56,910 --> 02:08:00,400
- How did it happen?
- We don't know, sir.

930
02:08:00,400 --> 02:08:04,190
There are Muslim hair on him and lots
of scars on his body.

931
02:08:06,180 --> 02:08:08,340
Sofia...

932
02:08:08,340 --> 02:08:10,170
Does Sofia know this?

933
02:08:10,170 --> 02:08:15,280
Princess Sofia is dining with Alişar Bey.
She doesn't know yet.

934
02:08:15,280 --> 02:08:18,650
- Good.
- What are your orders?

935
02:08:18,650 --> 02:08:26,170
Dress Kalonoz with his own clothes. Then
he should go to Alişar and Sofia.

936
02:08:28,040 --> 02:08:35,480
Alişar Bey shall see the Turks cruelty
and how noncompliant they are.

937
02:08:44,180 --> 02:08:49,330
From this day on, I promise you
for your safety, Princess.

938
02:08:49,830 --> 02:08:53,830
Besides, I ordered another caravan
for you.

939
02:08:54,030 --> 02:09:00,210
They should be here soon. Caravans, and
your counters at the bazaar...

940
02:09:00,210 --> 02:09:02,410
... are under my protection.

941
02:09:03,760 --> 02:09:09,860
The support of a powerful Banner Lord
like you always make us happy.

942
02:09:11,670 --> 02:09:13,740
But...

943
02:09:15,590 --> 02:09:21,790
... if Edebali dominates the bazaar, that
will be bad for all of us.

944
02:09:23,970 --> 02:09:27,450
Edebali and dominating the bazaar...

945
02:09:30,160 --> 02:09:33,230
Not possible while I'm around, Princess.

946
02:09:35,270 --> 02:09:39,000
Edebali and his Ahis will get the
bazaar moving.

947
02:09:39,790 --> 02:09:43,590
But, under my shadow.

948
02:09:45,080 --> 02:09:49,080
And as long as we gain something
from them.

949
02:09:55,550 --> 02:09:58,950
How will you stop them?

950
02:11:40,780 --> 02:11:42,660
How?

951
02:11:43,670 --> 02:11:46,330
He was ambushed while returning
to the castle.

952
02:11:46,710 --> 02:11:48,530
Who would do this?

953
02:11:49,140 --> 02:11:51,420
He was fighting the Turks.

954
02:11:56,470 --> 02:12:00,710
Osman! Osman did this, I know it!

955
02:12:02,580 --> 02:12:06,500
This attack was not just aimed at us.

956
02:12:06,820 --> 02:12:11,190
This is an uprising which disregards you,
Alişar Bey.

957
02:12:17,580 --> 02:12:20,800
I want Osman's life.

958
02:12:36,410 --> 02:12:40,690
"Valiants don't protect dishonest ones."
I said.

959
02:12:43,590 --> 02:12:45,860
He turned, looked...

960
02:12:47,950 --> 02:12:50,410
... then smiled in such a way that...

961
02:12:50,590 --> 02:12:57,910
... my ancestors from the savannas flash
right before my eyes.

962
02:13:00,620 --> 02:13:02,820
He looked at me in such a way that...

963
02:13:03,330 --> 02:13:08,540
... he had Hamza's looks in Uhud.

964
02:13:09,880 --> 02:13:12,200
Why didn't you say "Stop."?

965
02:13:12,200 --> 02:13:15,880
Who tells someone who's going to holy
war to stop, you fool?

966
02:13:15,880 --> 02:13:22,160
"Go!" you say! So he doesn't worry about
the ones left behind!

967
02:13:22,160 --> 02:13:28,690
"Go!" you say. So that their essence
leaves their body!

968
02:13:33,740 --> 02:13:37,740
"Don't leave my Osman alone." I said.

969
02:13:39,370 --> 02:13:46,420
Just so we can call these lands, which
bullies like you wander about, home...

970
02:13:48,740 --> 02:13:51,360
... sacrifice yourself, I said.

971
02:13:56,130 --> 02:14:00,670
He's gone. He's gone.

972
02:14:05,830 --> 02:14:08,260
He's gone.

973
02:14:12,540 --> 02:14:14,620
He didn't come ever again.

974
02:14:22,130 --> 02:14:26,610
He made his father, a martyr's father.

975
02:14:30,390 --> 02:14:38,390
He made the lands his gravestone is
laid upon, our home.

976
02:14:45,180 --> 02:14:50,710
"Valiants don't protect dishonest ones."
I said.

977
02:14:50,710 --> 02:14:53,100
It's time to stay alarmed.

978
02:14:56,060 --> 02:14:59,000
Bamsı is a martyr's father!

979
02:15:00,500 --> 02:15:04,710
Bamsı is a martyr's father! Bamsı has
become a martyr's father!

980
02:15:10,810 --> 02:15:13,250
Now...

981
02:15:30,160 --> 02:15:35,560
Now it's time.

982
02:15:40,850 --> 02:15:44,850
Thank Allah a thousand times...

983
02:15:45,600 --> 02:15:49,300
... I will take my son Aybars' revenge.

984
02:16:48,280 --> 02:16:51,980
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim
(In the name of Allah, the merciful and compassionate.)

985
02:16:53,260 --> 02:16:55,500
Bamsı Bey!

986
02:17:00,100 --> 02:17:02,790
I don't want to die without
becoming a Muslim.

987
02:17:31,560 --> 02:17:34,200
My love.

988
02:17:34,200 --> 02:17:36,590
I will take your revenge.

989
02:17:38,400 --> 02:17:46,060
I swear, I won't let Osman go without
making him pay for this!

990
02:18:28,610 --> 02:18:34,490
Kalonoz's spirit will reach peace when we
reach our goals, my daughter.

991
02:18:35,890 --> 02:18:42,210
My dear daughter Sofia, we'll hold tight
to take Kalonoz's...

992
02:18:42,210 --> 02:18:44,260
... and other fallen ones' revenges.

993
02:18:44,510 --> 02:18:49,660
In our cause, what suits us is not
shedding tears...

994
02:18:49,660 --> 02:18:53,710
... but holding on tightly against those
who did this.

995
02:19:12,430 --> 02:19:15,750
We will make them pay for this!

996
02:19:26,310 --> 02:19:32,430
Now that I saw you side by side like the
mountains, I am happy.

997
02:19:32,430 --> 02:19:35,220
And Allah shall make you happy.

998
02:19:39,910 --> 02:19:43,710
The enemy set traps like the
weasels they are.

999
02:19:43,930 --> 02:19:51,210
But thankfully, my brother Osman was
there to save me with his claws.

1000
02:19:51,210 --> 02:19:54,450
We did, for now, brother.

1001
02:19:56,920 --> 02:20:03,600
We shall stay no more, uncle. Wolves to
wolves, dogs to dogs.

1002
02:20:04,480 --> 02:20:07,410
Everyone learned the truth.

1003
02:20:07,700 --> 02:20:13,310
The snakes in Kulucahisar, that Banner
Lord in Eskihisar...

1004
02:20:13,310 --> 02:20:15,630
... are our enemies.

1005
02:20:15,630 --> 02:20:19,140
What does Alişar Bey have to do
with this, Osman?

1006
02:20:20,470 --> 02:20:24,080
Your aunt is right, my nephew. And don't
you know?

1007
02:20:24,080 --> 02:20:27,280
Soon a wedding tent will be established.

1008
02:20:28,310 --> 02:20:33,380
Before Alişar attacked the Tent, he
talked with Sofia in his mansion.

1009
02:20:37,940 --> 02:20:41,940
It's obvious who filled him with
the anger.

1010
02:20:49,070 --> 02:20:52,490
Osman! What are you saying, brother?

1011
02:21:00,630 --> 02:21:05,040
Yaman! Drums are being played.
Who is coming?

1012
02:21:19,820 --> 02:21:22,460
Your death is here, Dündar Bey!

1013
02:21:26,480 --> 02:21:33,210
Things have gone out of control. What do
you think you're doing Alişar Bey?

1014
02:21:36,040 --> 02:21:40,040
Ask that to Osman, not me!

1015
02:21:47,790 --> 02:21:52,790
Osman, I'm arresting you for killing the
Kulucahisar Castle's Commander Kalonoz.

1016
02:21:53,210 --> 02:23:09,430
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com